<p>Studio portraiture and photojournalism both assumed great prominence in =
these decades, whether by offering empowering representations of ordinary s=
ubjects or shedding light on struggles for justice and human rights. In 196=
9, meanwhile, filmmaker Sarah Maldoror (1929=E2=80=932020) produced her fir=
st short film, <em>Monangamb=C3=A9=C3=A9=C3=A9</em>, which captured the ess=
ence of struggles for equality in the nation of Angola.</p>

