            <figcaption>
                            <div class=3D"f-caption-title">
                    <div>
                                                    <p>Still from <em>Monan=
gamb=C3=A9=C3=A9=C3=A9</em>, 1969<br class=3D"softbreak"></p>
                                            </div>
                </div> <br>
                                        <div class=3D" f-caption"><p>Sarah =
Maldoror<br class=3D"softbreak"></p></div>
                                </figcaption>
    </figure>
<p>The film contributed to broader discourses about the role of the moving =
image in shaping Pan-African activism and cultural expression. Maldoror=E2=
=80=99s twin emphases on popular will and personal self-invention reverbera=
te in the films presented in this series, as they address the past and the =
popular as intertwined sources for inspiration and as a means to envision o=
ur shared world.</p><p>The films will be screened according to the followin=
g schedule:</p><p>Aug 10=E2=80=93Sep 16<br class=3D"softbreak">Larry Achiam=
pong=E2=80=99s&nbsp;<em>Relic Traveller: Phase 1&nbsp;</em>(2017) and M=C3=
=B3nica de Miranda=E2=80=99s&nbsp;<em>Path to the Stars</em>&nbsp;(2022)</p=
><p>Sep 19=E2=80=93Oct 28<br class=3D"softbreak">Sammy Baloji=E2=80=99s&nbs=
p;<em>AEQUARE: The Future That Never Was </em>(2023)</p><p>Oct 31=E2=80=93D=
ec 2<br class=3D"softbreak">Steffani Jemison=E2=80=99s&nbsp;<em>The Meaning=
 of Various Photographs to Tyrand Needham</em>&nbsp;(2009=E2=80=9310)</p><p=
>Dec 5=E2=80=93Jan 6<br class=3D"softbreak">Sarah Maldoror=E2=80=99s&nbsp;<=
em>Monangamb=C3=A9=C3=A9=C3=A9&nbsp;</em>(1968) and&nbsp;<em>And the Dogs K=
ept Silent </em>(1978)</p><p>Surrounding the screening room, a film-like ri=
bbon of approximately two dozen studio and press photographs shows scenes o=
f public life from the mid-20th century and more recently.<br class=3D"soft=
break"></p>

<span class=3D"hr"></span>

<p><em>Screens: A Panafrica Film Series</em> is curated by Antawan I. Byrd,=
 associate curator of Photography and Media, Art Institute of Chicago, and =
assistant professor of Art History, Northwestern University; Adom Getachew,=
 professor of Political Science and Race, Diaspora, and Indigeneity, Univer=
sity of Chicago; and Matthew Witkovsky, Richard and Ellen Sandor Chair and =
Curator, Photography and Media, and vice president for strategic art initia=
tives.<br class=3D"softbreak"></p>



